# Challenge 4: Complete CRUD Operations
 
## Summary
 
Implements missing PUT and DELETE endpoints for campaigns and ad slots, fixes the broken `POST /api/ad-slots`, and closes a fallback role assignment gap in `authMiddleware`. All new endpoints inherit the authentication and ownership patterns established in Challenge 3.
 
## What Changed
 
### Auth middleware (`apps/backend/src/auth.ts`)
- Reject authenticated users with neither a Sponsor nor Publisher record — previously they received a fallback PUBLISHER role, which could incorrectly pass publisher auth checks
- Now returns `401` immediately if no ownership context exists after session validation
 
### Campaign routes (`apps/backend/src/routes/campaigns.ts`)
- Added `PUT /api/campaigns/:id` — verifies ownership via `campaignId === req.user.sponsorId`, returns `404` if not found, `403` if not owned, `200` with updated campaign on success
- Added `DELETE /api/campaigns/:id` — same ownership check, returns `204` on success
 
### Ad slot routes (`apps/backend/src/routes/adSlots.ts`)
- Fixed `POST /api/ad-slots` — removed non-existent schema fields (`dimensions`, `pricingModel`), derives `publisherId` from session instead of `req.body`
- Added `PUT /api/ad-slots/:id` — verifies ownership via `adSlot.publisherId === req.user.publisherId`, returns `404`/`403`/`200`
- Added `DELETE /api/ad-slots/:id` — same ownership pattern, returns `204`
 
## Why
 
The previous implementation had TODO stubs for all four mutating routes. The `POST /api/ad-slots` handler was referencing fields that don't exist in the Prisma schema (`dimensions`, `pricingModel`) causing runtime errors on creation, and was accepting `publisherId` from `req.body` rather than the session.
 
## Verification
 
### Static checks
```bash
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
pnpm build
```
 
### Campaign CRUD (run as sponsor in browser console)
```javascript
// POST — create
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/campaigns', {
  method: 'POST',
  credentials: 'include',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    name: 'Test Campaign',
    budget: 5000,
    startDate: '2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z',
    endDate: '2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z',
  }),
}).then(r => r.json()).then(console.log);
// Expected: 201 with campaign object, sponsorId from session
 
// PUT — update
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/campaigns/<id>', {
  method: 'PUT',
  credentials: 'include',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Updated', budget: 7500 }),
}).then(r => r.json()).then(console.log);
// Expected: 200 with updated campaign
 
// DELETE
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/campaigns/<id>', {
  method: 'DELETE',
  credentials: 'include',
}).then(r => console.log(r.status));
// Expected: 204
```
 
### Ad slot CRUD (run as publisher in browser console)
```javascript
// POST — create
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/ad-slots', {
  method: 'POST',
  credentials: 'include',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    name: 'Test Banner',
    type: 'DISPLAY',
    basePrice: 750,
    width: 728,
    height: 90,
  }),
}).then(r => r.json()).then(console.log);
// Expected: 201 with ad slot object, publisherId from session
 
// PUT — update
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/ad-slots/<id>', {
  method: 'PUT',
  credentials: 'include',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name: 'Test Banner Updated', basePrice: 900 }),
}).then(r => r.json()).then(console.log);
// Expected: 200 with updated ad slot
 
// DELETE
await fetch('http://localhost:4291/api/ad-slots/<id>', {
  method: 'DELETE',
  credentials: 'include',
}).then(r => console.log(r.status));
// Expected: 204
```
 
### Authorization checks
| Scenario | Expected |
|---|---|
| Publisher accessing sponsor's campaign | 403 |
| Sponsor accessing publisher's ad slot mutation | 403 |
| Any request without session cookie | 401 |
| Non-existent resource ID | 404 |
| User with no sponsor/publisher record | 401 |
